const BU3832_R19_EDITS=[{"topic":"jesusbirth","oldQ":"Which elderly man rejoiced at seeing Jesus in the temple?","changes":{"q":"Which man at the temple praised God after seeing the young Jesus?","explanation":"Luke 2:25–32 names Simeon as a righteous and devout man who praised God on seeing Jesus. The account does not specify his age."},"reason":"Luke 2 identifies Simeon without giving his age"},{"topic":"prophecy","oldQ":"Which prophet foretold that a virgin would become pregnant and bear a son called Immanuel?","changes":{"q":"Which prophet recorded the sign of a young woman giving birth to a son called Immanuel?","ref":"Isaiah 7:14; Matthew 1:22–23","explanation":"Isaiah 7:14 in the New World Translation speaks of a young woman who would bear a son called Immanuel; Matthew 1:22–23 quotes this prophecy using the expression “the virgin.” The prophet was Isaiah."},"reason":"Distinguishes 2013 NWT Isaiah wording and Matthew quotation"},{"id":43,"topic":"cain","oldQ":"Which brother cared for a flock of sheep?","changes":{"q":"What did Jehovah provide so that Cain would not be killed by someone who found him?","choices":["A sign for Cain","An army of guards","A wall around his fields","A ship to flee the region"],"ref":"Genesis 4:15","explanation":"After Cain expressed fear that someone might kill him, Jehovah established a sign for Cain so that someone finding him would not strike him down. Genesis 4:15 does not describe the sign’s appearance."},"reason":"Overlap with #39, which also asks about Abel’s occupation."},{"id":154,"topic":"joshua","oldQ":"What choice did Joshua urge the Israelites to make near the end of his life?","changes":{"q":"What did Joshua urge the Israelites to remove from among them?","choices":["Foreign gods","The Ark of the Covenant","The book of the Law","The priests at Shiloh"],"ref":"Joshua 24:23","explanation":"After Israel said it would serve Jehovah, Joshua urged the people to remove the foreign gods from among them and incline their hearts to Jehovah."},"reason":"This and #155 both revolve around Joshua 24:15; distinct angles but risk repeated experience."},{"id":163,"topic":"gideon","oldQ":"What did Gideon overhear in the enemy camp?","changes":{"q":"What did Gideon overhear a Midianite explaining in the enemy camp?","explanation":"Gideon overheard one Midianite relate a dream and another explain its significance for Gideon’s victory. The exchange strengthened Gideon’s confidence."},"reason":"Original “an interpretation of a dream” is correct but imprecise as to whether it is the dream or interpretation. The suggested wording makes the event clear."},{"id":195,"topic":"ruth","oldQ":"Whose God did Ruth choose as her own?","changes":{"q":"What did Naomi do when she saw Ruth was determined to accompany her?","choices":["She stopped trying to persuade Ruth","She ordered Ruth to return to Moab","She sent Ruth ahead alone","She refused to enter Bethlehem"],"ref":"Ruth 1:18","explanation":"When Naomi saw that Ruth was determined to accompany her, she stopped trying to persuade Ruth to turn back."},"reason":"Same passage tested repeatedly in #179/#190/#194."},{"id":452,"topic":"paul","oldQ":"Who was a seller of purple and a believer in Philippi?","changes":{"q":"Which seller of purple from Thyatira listened to Paul in Philippi?","explanation":"Acts 16:14 identifies Lydia as a seller of purple from Thyatira who listened as Paul spoke; she and her household were baptized."},"reason":"The answer Lydia is supported. “a believer in Philippi” is slightly loose because the account explicitly introduces Lydia as a worshipper of God and a seller of purple from Thyatira; then describes her response and baptism."},{"id":551,"topic":"psalms","oldQ":"Who will no longer be found according to Psalm 37:10?","changes":{"choices":["The wicked","The upright","The meek","Those who wait for Jehovah"],"explanation":"Psalm 37:10 says that the wicked will be no more. The psalm contrasts their fate with the future of the meek and the righteous."},"reason":"The wicked are specified by verse 10; violent people can also be wicked, making the alternative semantically fuzzy."},{"id":859,"topic":"christianliving","oldQ":"Which quality of the spirit is listed alongside kindness and goodness?","changes":{"choices":["Faith","Knowledge","Boldness","Wisdom"],"explanation":"Galatians 5:22–23 includes faith in the fruitage of the spirit, together with love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, mildness, and self-control."},"reason":"Round 12: compared with the official 2013 NWT chapter; keyed answer supported, editorial context/variety work remains."}];
